## Section A — Internal Guide (for Winfred)

**Data you hold on a lead, mapped to system:**

| Category | System |
|---|---|
| Name, phone, email | `~/real-estate-agent/clients/[slug]/profile.md`, `clients.db`, `wa-lead-queue.jsonl` |
| Conversation history | WhatsApp bridge `messages.db`, `wa-history.md` |
| Property interests / financial indicators | `profile.md`, `plan.md`, `clients.db` |
| Booking data | Calendly (cloud) + Google Calendar |
| Email correspondence | Gmail / Google Drive |
| Website form submissions | Neon Postgres DB + Vercel logs |
| Drip/newsletter subscription | `drip-subscribers.jsonl`, Neon Postgres |
| Telegram bot interactions | `~/.claude/state/` bot logs |
| n8n workflow execution logs | n8n instance |

**Retention carve-outs (cannot delete):**
- Completed transaction records: must keep **5 years** under CEA / Estate Agents Act — but this applies only to transacted clients, not unconverted leads.
- IRAS records: 5 years for property transaction documents.

**10-step deletion checklist** covers: local Mac files → WhatsApp bridge SQLite → Gmail/Drive/Calendar → Calendly → Telegram → PropertyGuru/99.co (advise them to request directly) → Canva → Neon/Vercel → n8n → document and confirm.

