## Section B — Draft Response to the Lead

Ready to send via WhatsApp or email:

> Hi [Name],
>
> Thank you for reaching out. Under PDPA, I'm happy to provide full transparency.
>
> **What I may hold:** Name, phone, email, enquiry details (property, budget, timeline), WhatsApp conversation history, meeting booking details (Calendly), and website form submissions.
>
> **Where it's stored:** My work computer (local files and database), Google Workspace (Gmail/Calendar), Calendly, and the WhatsApp bridge I use for client conversations. If your enquiry came via PropertyGuru or 99.co, they hold their own copy independently.
>
> **Data Access Request:** Email me at winfredquekoc@gmail.com with subject "PDPA Data Access Request — [Your Name]". I'll respond within 10 business days.
>
> **Deletion Request:** Email with subject "PDPA Deletion Request — [Your Name]". I'll delete from all systems I control within 10 business days and confirm in writing. Note: if we completed a transaction, CEA requires me to retain transaction records for 5 years — everything else would be deleted.
>
> For PropertyGuru/99.co data, contact them directly at dpo@propertyguru.com.sg.
>
> Warm regards,
> Winfred Quek | CEA R073319H | PropNex Realty

